WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.468
The CIA is now trying

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.870
to recruit Russian spies pretty openly.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.972
The agency dropping an emotional

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.108
two minute long video just last night

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:10.143
targeting disgruntled Russians

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:10.844
Their goal,

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.544
persuade them

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.645
to share any secrets

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.714
or sensitive information they may have.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.182
That could help the CIA.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:16.883
CNN senior

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.585
national security correspondent

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.552
Alex Marquardt is joining us

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.653
live from Washington.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.555
Alex, you got an exclusive interview

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.624
with CIA officials about these efforts.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.525
What exactly is it

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.027
that they're doing here?

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:27.660
That's right, Caitlin.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.728
And we also got an early

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:29.462
look at this video.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.430
Now, the CIA officials

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.231
I sat down with,

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.332
they told me that they see

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:33.867
Russia's war in Ukraine

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:34.567
as a rare,

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.469
even historic opportunity

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.438
to recruit more Russian spies.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.773
Now they're taking their efforts

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.440
up a notch

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.308
with this new recruitment video

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.710
trying to communicate to Russians

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.412
who have sensitive information.

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.746
We know what you're going through

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.681
and what you have is valuable.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.049
Caitlin

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.483
they're even quoting Tolstoy

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.851
and Dostoyevsky

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.786
to try to convince them

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.120
to get in touch with the CIA.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.758
At the television

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.927
factory in Eastern

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.396
Ghouta, raising

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.532
questions, being asked in Russian

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:08.001
in a new dramatic video by the CIA

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.903
just released to try to recruit

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.371
more Russian spies

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.639
by appealing to Russians

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.641
patriotism, frustrations

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.408
and the oppression

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:18.812
they face under the Putin regime.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.047
CIA officials told CNN

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.449
in an exclusive interview

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.417
that the war in Ukraine has created

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.453
an unprecedented opportunity

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.720
that they want to capitalize

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.923
on to recruit new Russian assets.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.357
Disaffection with the war

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.125
will continue

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.327
to gnaw away at the Russian leadership

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.396
beneath the steady diet of state

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.665
propaganda and practiced repression

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.767
In the past year of the war.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.969
The CIA has been encouraging Russians

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.504
with valuable information

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.472
to contact them

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:48.274
quietly, securely and anonymously.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.410
Through a portal on the dark web.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.212
We're looking around the world

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:53.580
for Russians

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.516
who are is disgusted with that is we are

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.984
because we're open for business

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.552
instructions have been posted

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.888
on the CIA's social media accounts.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.156
And this new video

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.125
after making an emotional pitch

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.192
to Russian viewers.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.961
Details how to do that

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.296
using the dark web browser called Tor.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.731
You're not powerless.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.200
It says Contact us in a safe way.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.002
The CIA recruitment video

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:16.970
was first posted

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.571
Monday evening on Telegram.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:19.739
The social media app

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.741
that is highly popular among Russians

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:24.444
who can't easily access unfiltered news

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.146
or other social media sites.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.915
I call it hanging out the shingle

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:29.816
and spreading the word

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.317
far and wide that

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.685
us in counterintelligence

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.721
is open for business.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.289
And we have deep pockets

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.390
and we want to strike

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.491
back against this man.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.593
You hate Vladimir Putin.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.128
You have an opportunity now to do it

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:42.662
safely.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.931
CIA officials told CNN they hope

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.032
the video will resonate

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.367
beyond intelligence

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.568
and security officials

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:49.102
with people

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.103
who may not realize

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.871
that they have sensitive information

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:52.505
to share,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.840
working, for example,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.643
in cyber tech, finance and other fields.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.678
They may think contacting the CIA

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.747
is too difficult or too dangerous.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.315
The CIA telling CNN

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.083
they want to demystify that.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:04.884
We need people

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.487
all through the Russian economy

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:08.855
to cooperate with us.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.890
We need to know what's going on

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.559
in this adversary country.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.361
There is no direct mention

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.896
of Putin or Ukraine.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.932
Nor CIA officials insist.

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.467
Is it meant to fuel unrest in Russia?

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.902
Rather, they tell CNN

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.504
these are timeless themes

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:25.071
that they hope

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.139
will drive Russians

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.508
into the arms of the CIA

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.643
at the CW, get money out of Syria.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.746
Every state

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.149
in every state

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.284
can read this, doing that.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:41.588
Look at that in my eastern

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.523
And the CIA says that their campaign

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:44.090
so far

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.425
during this war to recruit

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.659
new spies, disaffected

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.595
Russians, has been successful.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:50.096
They won't say to what degree

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.965
or how many people they have recruited.

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.766
But one CIA official told me,

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:54.767
in his words,

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.369
there's contact coming in

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.737
and they say they wouldn't

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:58.371
be rolling out

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.906
this new recruitment video

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.308
if they hadn't already had some success.

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.143
Caitlin, huh? Fascinating.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.912
That was the most fascinating thing

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.747
in the morning. Alex, thank you.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.349
OUTFRONT now, Elina Polyakov,

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.683
she is a Russian foreign affairs

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.818
expert and the president

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:12.852
and ceo of the Center

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.121
for European Policy Analysis.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:15.822
So, Elina,

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:18.891
as you hear these recruitment videos,

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:19.626
which just to be clear

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:20.560
are going out on telegram

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.028
as Alex is reporting.

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.129
That is a place

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.064
where Russians spend a lot of time.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.299
That is the social media,

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.601
the predominant social media in Russia.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.670
So what do you hear

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.105
when you hear these videos

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.039
and the appeal

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:33.706
that they're making

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.041
to retain your dignity, to

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.242
take care of your family?

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:38.945
I mean, hearing

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.113
the Russian language

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:42.348
as being spoken in these videos just now,

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.117
I think is absolutely brilliant.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:44.617
Honestly,

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:45.985
there are so many Russians

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.521
that we will never, ever hear from

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.257
who are disappointed with the future

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.158
they see ahead of them,

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.893
which is a very, very bleak future

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.328
under President Putin.

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:56.362
And we'll never hear them

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:57.563
talk about this publicly

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:58.865
because people in Russia

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:01.067
are really deeply afraid

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.302
of the kind of punishment

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:03.236
that might come with saying

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.304
anything in public.

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:04.937
You know, let's remember,

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:05.672
this is a country

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.173
that will throw you in jail

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.275
for holding up a white sheet of paper

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:10.510
with no words on it.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.313
So I think this is an absolutely

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.782
brilliant ploy by the CIA

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.685
to see if we can get some informants,

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:20.653
average people

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.455
to cooperate with the United States.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:22.922
Now, Olena,

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.090
you heard what Alex is reporting.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.092
He's saying the CIA knows that in a sense

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:27.260
that they were on investment,

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.027
that they're doing this

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:28.795
because they

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.930
and they are having contacts already

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:31.998
coming in.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:33.566
Do you think to this point

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.401
about the risks

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.836
that the Russians are speaking to

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.905
or inside Russia who may see this

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.740
that this dark Web browser

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.008
that going to tour, that

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.710
this is something that

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.446
the people would take any enough people,

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:47.814
I guess, would take a risk on

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:50.149
Well, it's very hard

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:51.451
to strike the right tone.

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:52.518
You know, the kind of message

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:53.553
that we just heard in

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:54.420
the segment

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.622
is not going to appeal to everyone.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.591
Some people are going to laugh it off

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:00.159
but presumably

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.061
they get things out of cooperating

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.563
with the intelligence service this year.

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:05.331
They might get some payments.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:06.999
They might get security.

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:07.233
You know,

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.168
these are things that Russians

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:09.936
many Russians

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:11.671
are really craving right now.

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:14.140
So there is a certain appeal there.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:14.374
Is it

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.509
going to reach a large number of people?

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:17.877
We don't know.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:19.145
But I think the CIA is

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.880
probably counting on the fact that

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.148
even if it reaches

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:22.915
a few dozen

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:25.051
who take the necessary steps

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.753
and who feel comfortable doing that,

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:28.020
that's already a win.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.722
And Lina, one further question.

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.023
Alex was talking about the FBI

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.058
trying to recruit

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:32.525
people come

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:33.726
and going from the Russian embassy.

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.027
And it does make you realize

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.929
there are a lot of people

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:40.133
who who do find ways to come and go from

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:41.401
Russia in and out of the United States

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:43.069
that are here completely legally

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:44.003
that are able to do that.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:44.570
There are Russians

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.037
also come

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:46.105
and go from other places

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.039
in large numbers.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:47.473
Maybe, you know,

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:49.075
places in the United Arab

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.243
Emirates, for example.

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:53.913
Do you think that there's been success

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:55.748
in recruiting among that group?

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:58.651
Again, it's hard to know.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.552
We don't know what

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.554
the intelligence agencies are doing.

00:07:01.554 --> 00:07:02.221
They're not going to share

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:04.457
that kind of information with us.

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:05.458
But, of course,

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:06.125
there are many,

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:06.993
many Russians

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:07.860
who are still coming

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.362
to the United States as tourists.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.963
It's not easy to get a tourist visa.

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:12.498
Of course, for most Russians,

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:13.866
but those who have the

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:15.034
the money and the wealth

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:15.802
to travel

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:18.104
to go to a different country

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:19.772
besides Russia to get their visas,

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.174
basically impossible

00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:22.942
to get a visa to the United States

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.277
in Russia today.

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:25.111
But look, you

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:25.978
if you have a visa

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:28.214
to go to Germany or Estonia, it's

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:29.515
probably not that hard for you

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:31.517
if you're willing to to wait it out.

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:33.186
So I think certainly there's huge

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:34.153
opportunities here.

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:35.087
We know

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:36.422
that many, many Russians

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:38.825
especially those that are more well-off

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:40.026
who are in the middle

00:07:40.026 --> 00:07:41.461
class, you know,

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:43.062
who want a different kind of life

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:43.930
for themselves,

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.199
you know, are going to come to the US

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:48.734
and they want to live like Westerners.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:49.569
They don't want to live

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:50.703
in an oppressive society

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:52.104
with a bleak future.

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:53.473
All right, Alina, thank you very much.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:54.207
I appreciate it.

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:55.775
Thank you.

